    <!--
      Hindi (hi).

      NEEDS REVIEW BY A NATIVE SPEAKER BEFORE RELEASE. This app is used to explain insurance
      contracts to someone who is about to sign one, so a sentence that is merely plausible is not
      good enough here. Treat this as a solid first draft, not a shipped translation.

      Choices made deliberately, so a reviewer can disagree with them on purpose:

      - Respectful register throughout (आप, and -ें/-एँ imperatives). The agent is a professional
        addressing a client, and the client may well be older than them.
      - "साइन", "क्लाइंट", "PDF", "पेज" and "नोट" are kept as the loanwords Indian field agents
        actually use. "हस्ताक्षर" is correct but formal-legal, and it is also much longer, which
        matters for a label sharing half a folded screen with five others.
      - "पेज %1$d, कुल %2$d" rather than a literal "of", because "3 में से पेज 1" reads awkwardly
        and inverts the argument order.
    -->

